WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.650
- What do you feel like the best lesson,

00:00:01.650 --> 00:00:02.970
other than her being so supportive,

00:00:02.970 --> 00:00:04.320
I imagine you're like that with your kids

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:06.630
because you were taught
that from a young age,

00:00:06.630 --> 00:00:08.220
but what do you think the biggest lesson

00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:09.120
you got from her was?

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:10.200
- Oh, believe in yourself.

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:11.033
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:11.033 --> 00:00:12.630
- 'Cause we grew up in a
really poor neighborhood

00:00:12.630 --> 00:00:13.463
with not much.

00:00:13.463 --> 00:00:15.450
And you know, there was no
reason for me to believe

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:17.160
that I was gonna be here and make it.

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:19.050
But she always instilled
in me believe in yourself,

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:19.883
you could do whatever you want.

00:00:19.883 --> 00:00:23.339
And that, I instill that in
my kids and I believe it.

00:00:23.339 --> 00:00:24.912
- That's incredible.

00:00:24.912 --> 00:00:26.751
'Cause not all parents do
that, you know what I'm saying?

00:00:26.751 --> 00:00:27.584
- [Darius] Definitely not, I know.

00:00:27.584 --> 00:00:28.539
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:28.539 --> 00:00:29.488
- When I was a kid and she instilled in us

00:00:29.488 --> 00:00:32.070
that you help people, not
people that are less fortunate.

00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:33.030
You help people that need help.

00:00:33.030 --> 00:00:34.292
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:34.292 --> 00:00:35.640
- I tell this story about my
brother, I guess I was 10,

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:37.110
probably not 10, I was
probably seven or eight

00:00:37.110 --> 00:00:38.970
and my brother was 14 and he went to,

00:00:38.970 --> 00:00:41.010
we had this couple that
lived in our neighborhood

00:00:41.010 --> 00:00:42.567
and the husband was in the Navy.

00:00:42.567 --> 00:00:44.550
And so, he went away on the ship

00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:45.687
and the yard was growing up

00:00:45.687 --> 00:00:48.360
and my brother went home,
went over and cut her grass,

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:50.340
and she gave him $10.

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:52.500
And he came home bragging
about the $10 he got.

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:54.570
And my mom whooped his butt

00:00:54.570 --> 00:00:56.647
and told him, "You take that $10 back down

00:00:56.647 --> 00:00:57.967
"and you give it back to her

00:00:57.967 --> 00:00:59.377
"because we don't help people for money.

00:00:59.377 --> 00:01:00.780
"We help people to help people."

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:01.613
And that was just something.

00:01:01.613 --> 00:01:02.883
- Oh, wow.

00:01:03.775 --> 00:01:06.920
You got a great mom.

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:07.753
Wow.

00:01:07.753 --> 00:01:08.903
Very, very lucky.

00:01:08.903 --> 00:01:10.200
Well, we have a little surprise for you

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:11.160
and I was very excited

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:12.180
to be able to do this.
- Do ya?

00:01:12.180 --> 00:01:13.013
- Yeah, you don't know.

00:01:13.013 --> 00:01:13.860
He really doesn't know about it.

00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:15.697
This is not TV, this is real.

00:01:15.697 --> 00:01:19.350
For your many, many charitable
efforts over the years

00:01:19.350 --> 00:01:21.480
and for helping those who need help,

00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:24.807
CMA is actually honoring you
as Humanitarian of the Year.

00:01:24.807 --> 00:01:27.060
- Wow.
(audience cheering)

00:01:27.060 --> 00:01:28.083
Oh my goodness.

00:01:30.014 --> 00:01:31.203
Wow.

00:01:31.203 --> 00:01:33.118
- I was so excited.
- That's awesome.

00:01:33.118 --> 00:01:34.943
Wow.
(audience cheering)

00:01:34.943 --> 00:01:35.776
Wow.

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:38.705
I really did not know that.

00:01:38.705 --> 00:01:39.663
- I know.

00:01:39.663 --> 00:01:41.071
I was like, "No, he really doesn't know."

00:01:41.071 --> 00:01:42.171
- I did not know that.

